<section class="content-section" id="familiars" aria-labelledby="familiars-heading">
  <div class="section-header" data-reveal>
    <p class="section-kicker">Familiars</p>
    <h2 id="familiars-heading">From blank chatbox to agent workspace.</h2>
    <p>A familiar is not a faceless bot. It has a name, purpose, memory, toolset, voice, role, and a place in a workflow that continues after the chat ends.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card-grid three">
    <div class="glass-card" data-reveal>
      <p class="card-kicker">01 · Identity</p>
      <h3>Name the agent and define the work.</h3>
      <p>Give each familiar a clear purpose, tone, tools, and operating rules so it can show up as the right collaborator instead of a blank assistant.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="glass-card" data-reveal>
      <p class="card-kicker">02 · Memory</p>
      <h3>Keep the context that matters.</h3>
      <p>Project history, decisions, preferences, and working notes persist across sessions — continuity that's explicit, not trapped in a temporary chat.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="glass-card" data-reveal>
      <p class="card-kicker">03 · Tools</p>
      <h3>Let agents act through known surfaces.</h3>
      <p>Familiars connect to terminals, code workspaces, docs, messaging, and local runtimes through inspectable tool contracts you can review and replace.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
